WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.690
The first known disaster in the Final Destination
franchise takes place in Victorian England

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.890
in 1889, when rising gas from some underground
construction causes the explosion of a house

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:10.280
at Number 4 Mornington Crescent.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.511
Thanks to the vision of the young girl Juliet
Collins, there are seven survivors, but one

00:00:14.511 --> 00:00:16.400
by one, Death would reclaim them.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.590
Newsman Matthew Upton was impaled by a chemical
filled pipe, historians Hector Barnes, Jane

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:24.449
Stanley and their protégé Andrew are poisoned
by snakebite, surgeon Stewart Tubbs inhales

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:28.990
a poisonous gas and serial killer Bill Sangster
is caught in the gears of a drawbridge.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:32.840
These events are the first known example of
what I’ll be calling the Flight 180 phenomenon,

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.300
where accident survivors are picked off one
by one after avoiding Death.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.120
This usually happens when a clairvoyant, a
character with an ability to foresee future

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.829
events, has a vision of his or her own death
and saves their own life, and possibly the

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:47.980
lives of others, forcing Death to change its
ways to reclaim its rightful victims.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.050
There is a lot of mystery surrounding Death.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:53.450
Is Death just a force of nature, no different
than time or gravity?

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:57.350
Or is it an entity, a grim reaper with it’s
own thoughts, plans and vulnerabilities?

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:01.820
In this video I’ll be analyzing every death
in the series, including the ones that occur

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.949
off screen, in the novels and in the comics.

00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:08.140
This video is sponsored by Hunt a Killer.

00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:12.270
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:15.810
Before I continue on with the history of Death,
which is essentially the Final Destination

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.609
timeline, here are a couple of disclaimers.

00:01:17.609 --> 00:01:20.039
For this video, I’ll be using the sequel
timeline.

00:01:20.039 --> 00:01:24.409
In the first Final Destination movie, we see
that Flight 180 crashed on May 13, 1999.

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:28.970
However, in the sequels, that date has been
moved to May 13th, 2000, and I’ve theorized

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:32.181
that this has something to do with the line
in the first movie, where Alex looks up at

00:01:32.181 --> 00:01:35.200
the stars and wonders if there could be a
world where the Flight 180 passengers are

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.359
still safe.

00:01:36.359 --> 00:01:39.499
Second disclaimer -- there is at least one
premonition incident that we don’t know

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:42.460
the details of that occurs before the other
accidents.

00:01:43.921 --> 00:01:46.869
“It’s just that I’ve seen this before.

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:55.499
A lucky few survive a disaster, and
one by one Death comes for them all.”

00:01:55.499 --> 00:01:58.619
I’ve theorized that this could be William
Bludworth’s own near-death experience, but

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:00.960
as of right now, we don’t know for sure.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:01.960
Third disclaimer.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.179
Outside of the movies, there are also Final
Destination novels and comics.

00:02:04.179 --> 00:02:07.979
While they don’t seem to directly contradict
the canon of the movies from what I can tell,

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:09.149
they are out of print.

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:12.209
Not having access to all of them, it’s hard
to say when they all take place chronologically,

00:02:12.209 --> 00:02:14.900
so I’ll start with the ones that I can’t
place in the timeline.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.597
With that all being said, let’s get into
it.

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:26.790
In Final Destination: Dead Reckoning, punk
rock singer Jess Golden saves some lives with

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.569
her vision of a collapsing nightclub.

00:02:28.569 --> 00:02:32.170
The bouncer Sebastian, is later killed by
his exploding motorcycle, a student named

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:36.560
Amber is run over by an out of control car,
a jock named Charlie falls down an elevator

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.430
shaft, a cop named Marina is poisoned by a
black widow, a waitress named Macy is struck

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:44.469
by a metal pane, an alcoholic named Ben falls
into a manhole, and a drug dealer named Eric

00:02:44.469 --> 00:02:46.060
is hit in the head with a surfboard.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.489
The book also describes what is perhaps the
only visual depiction of Death’s true form.

00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:54.980
In Jess’s dreams, she sees a horrific monstrosity
of shifting bones and corpses that supposedly

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.400
represent Death.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.939
Several months later, Jess and her friend
Jamie are nowhere to be found, so it’s unknown

00:02:59.939 --> 00:03:01.609
if they found a way to beat death.

00:03:01.609 --> 00:03:06.329
In Final Destination: Destination Zero, journalist
Patti Fuller learns she had a great grandmother

00:03:06.329 --> 00:03:09.709
who once cheated death by being revived after
she drowned in a river.

00:03:09.709 --> 00:03:13.360
Patti had her own vision, and foresaw the
bombing of the South Hill Metroline in Los

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.360
Angeles.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.129
She managed to get some people off the train
before it happened.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:19.790
The survivors include Hal, who later drowned
in a flash flood, Zack, a construction man

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:23.739
who was cut in half by a glass pane, and Susan,
a mechanic who was burned to death.

00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:27.819
Then there was Al, who was beheaded by a flying
hubcap while receiving what I will refer to

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:31.123
as mobile pipe cleaning service by a professional…

00:03:31.123 --> 00:03:34.070
named Candi, and Will who was impaled by CDs

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.599
and DVDs from a now defunct electronics store.

00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:38.870
I’m guessing that is NOT just what he needed.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.620
"You're just what I needed!"

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.790
Patti eventually dies of an intentional overdose
so that she can be revived, and theoretically

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.931
go on living just as her great grandmother
once did many years ago.

00:03:47.931 --> 00:03:52.279
In Final Destination: End of the Line, recent
high school grad Danny King has a vision about

00:03:52.279 --> 00:03:54.829
a train crash at 32nd Street in New York City.

00:03:54.829 --> 00:03:58.450
This time, the survivors include Rinoka, who
is crushed by a bathtub that falls through

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:02.549
the floor; Peter, who is impaled by the horns
of a gazelle; Jack, who falls onto a wine

00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:06.400
corkscrew that impaled him in the eye; Mary-Beth,
who is butchered by a chainsaw dropped by

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.349
a construction worker; and Bodil and James,
who are both part of a wild series of events

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:13.569
culminating in them being thrown from the
top of a moving truck into a store display

00:04:13.569 --> 00:04:15.269
of umbrellas that impale them.

00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:17.959
The last two remaining are Danny and his sister,
Louise.

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:21.590
What happens to them is very interesting,
and potentially exhibits another rarely seen

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:22.840
ability of Death.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:26.389
Louise tries to do what Patti Fuller did,
so she can technically die by injection but

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:27.389
be revived.

00:04:27.389 --> 00:04:30.319
“Only new life can defeat Death.”

00:04:30.319 --> 00:04:34.560
But when Louise comes back, she accidentally
cuts the brakes while adjusting her brother’s

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.860
motorbike, and in his final moments, Danny
realizes that Louise was only revived in order

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.370
to play a part in his Death.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:44.300
This is significant because it means Death
has the ability to use the victims’ survival

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.949
tactics against them -- however, this alone
is not enough to prove that Death is a conscious

00:04:48.949 --> 00:04:50.980
entity, rather than a natural phenomenon.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:55.270
What happens to Louise afterwards is not known,
but the next novel, Final Destination: Dead

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:59.300
Man’s Hand would introduce a new facet that
would change our perception about Death in

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:02.250
the Final Destination franchise.

