00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.949
The next novel is Final Destination: Dead
Man’s Hand.

00:06:12.949 --> 00:06:17.050
Allie Goodwin gets married to her ex-boyfriend
one drunk night in Vegas and saves five lives

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:20.770
when she foresees the glass elevator collapse
in a hotel called Merlin’s Tower.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:24.669
Sure enough, Death comes for all of the escapees,
but unlike all of the disasters mentioned

00:06:24.669 --> 00:06:28.690
so far, they do not die in the same order
they died in during the premonition, and this

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.530
is because of another rule of Death.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:34.599
If someone intervenes with Death’s plans
and saves a life, that person will be “skipped”,

00:06:34.599 --> 00:06:37.660
but Death will come back around for them after
completing its list.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.380
Because of this, it starts with an exotic
dancer named Shawna who is rammed into a slot

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.900
machine by a special prize car that rolled
off of it’s display platform.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.720
Guess it wasn’t her lucky day at the slots.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:50.830
Her boyfriend, a man named Warren Ackerman,
dies shortly thereafter when a powerline falls

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:52.380
onto a puddle he’s standing in.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:58.080
Then a gambling addict named Arlen is killed
during… a pipe cleaning disaster… involving

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.080
a severed pipe.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:02.610
Death seems to have preferred methods of taking
people out, and I guess in the books it really

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:06.409
likes to… interrupt that clarinet practice…

00:07:06.409 --> 00:07:10.470
Allie’s newlywed husband Thomas is hit by
a speeding truck, another commonly used tactic

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:13.970
of the reaper, but Allie’s death is much
less in line with the usual methods found

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.770
in the world of Final Destination.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:19.620
After her initial premonition, she was sprayed
with blood by one of the victims she was unable

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.189
to save from the elevator, and once she is
the last remaining survivor, she finds out

00:07:23.189 --> 00:07:25.340
that she contracted HIV from that blood.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:28.639
We don’t see her death, but it’s heavily
implied that she does not survive.

00:07:28.639 --> 00:07:32.689
This is perhaps the only subtle death among
those who cheated Death’s design.

00:07:32.689 --> 00:07:36.289
I think William Bludworth’s explanation
is the best answer as to why so many of them

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:38.250
pass on in such a gruesome manner.

00:07:39.791 --> 00:07:47.690
“The risk of cheating the plan, of disrespecting
the design, could incite a fury that could

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.531
terrorize even the grim reaper.

00:07:50.531 --> 00:07:54.189
And you don’t even want to **** with that
mack-daddy!”

00:07:54.189 --> 00:07:58.039
I think the basic implication is that if you
mess up Death’s original plan for you it’s

00:07:58.039 --> 00:08:01.460
gonna be much scarier when your fate finally
does catch up with you.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:05.090
Final Destination: Sacrifice is an interesting
departure from the standard formula, because

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.210
the protagonist has many prophetic visions.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:10.819
The first is a bus accident, but he’s unable
to convince anyone else to get off the bus,

00:08:10.819 --> 00:08:12.360
and he is the only survivor.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.830
Next, he sees a factory explosion, and this
time he’s able to save himself and four

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:20.229
co-workers, but soon finds he has only delayed
each of their appointments with death.

00:08:20.229 --> 00:08:24.770
After a ladder accident, a bathtub electrocution,
a lawn mower malfunction and a railroad splattering,

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.189
he once again finds himself the only survivor.

00:08:27.189 --> 00:08:30.950
Next, he envisions himself and his family
dying in a gas explosion.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:34.580
At this point he’s overwhelmed with grief,
and decides to hang himself, thinking that

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:39.100
if Death got what he wanted with him, the
people in his life would maybe no longer be in danger.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.870
There are two ways to look at this story.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:44.170
It could be that Death is not perfect, and
these first three attempts were unsuccessful,

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:47.360
or it could be that suicide was in the cards
for him all along.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:51.160
There are a few other disasters referenced
in news articles, but it’s not clear when

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:52.310
they take place.

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:56.550
They include a building collapse that kills
14, a bus crash that takes 32, an electrical

00:08:56.550 --> 00:09:00.570
fire that destroys an office, a capsized boat
resulting in the loss of 4 lives, a Ferris

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:05.080
wheel that sends 9 more souls to the afterlife,
an accident in the gulf that kills 18, a hardware

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:09.380
store accident that claims 2 (which we only
know to take place some time after April

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:10.380
of 2003).

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.660
That’s it for the ambiguously placed entries.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.910
If you know when some of these take place,
please do drop me a comment.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.940
From here on out, the order of events are
more clearly spelled out.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.140
Which takes us to the end of April 2000.

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:25.570
The office employees of a New York branch
of Presage Paper set out on a business retreat,

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:29.200
but as their bus crosses the North Bay Bridge,
the structure starts to collapse.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:32.970
A part time salesman named Sam Lawton has
a premonition, causing him to take his ex

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:35.340
girlfriend Molly Harper and flee the bus.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.620
Six others give chase, and as a result, they
are the only survivors.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:42.180
At the funeral for the deceased employees,
they encounter William Bludworth, who warns

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:45.950
them that Death does not like to be cheated,
and over the next couple days, each of them

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:48.070
would find out exactly what he means.

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:51.680
Intern Candice Hooper breaks her spine in
a freak gymnastics accident, tech expert Isaac

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:55.620
Palmer is taken out by a variety of accidents
during his massage therapy and board member

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:59.440
Olivia Castle falls out of a building after
having her vision impaired during a botched

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:00.440
Lasik surgery.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:04.720
The next on Death’s list is factory supervisor
Nathan Sears, but he’s able to avoid Death’s

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:07.540
attempt, and an employee named Roy Carson
takes the fall instead.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.610
According to William Bludworth’s theory,
this may have changed Nathan’s position

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.659
by adding Roy’s remaining lifespan to his
own.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:16.950
“You shorted Death.

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:21.570
So you let Death have somebody else in your
place, and then you take their spot in the

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:26.420
realm of the living -- all the days and years
they’ve let to live.

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:28.830
And they take your place in Death.”

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:32.280
We never find out if Bludworth is telling
the truth here though, because as it turns

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:35.220
out Roy only had a couple days left to live
anyway.

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:39.650
“Turns out Roy had an enlarged blood vessel
in his brain so big, it was about to burst.”

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:43.410
And Bludworth is also pretty adamant that
you can’t escape Death, so it seems quite

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:47.090
possible that this letting Death have someone
in your place business is just an unproven

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:48.650
theory that he’s testing.

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:51.480
Otherwise you’d probably have a bunch of
immortal serial killers running around the

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:53.010
world of Final Destination.

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:54.570
This is New York… not Haddonfield.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:58.800
It doesn’t take long for the boss, Dennis
Lapman, to be done in by a flying wrench.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:02.360
Sales manager Peter Friedkin decides to take
out Molly, hoping to gain her years, but ends

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:07.510
up settling for an FBI Agent named Block instead,
shortly before Sam finishes him off with a…

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:09.410
what is this thing called?

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:11.450
I’ll just call it a meat skewer.

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:15.140
On May 13th, 2000, Sam and Molly decide
to start a new life together in Paris, but

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:19.380
before their flight takes off, a 17 year old
student named Alex Browning has a vision.

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:23.381
He sees the plane malfunction and explode,
causing him to freak out and demand to be

00:11:23.381 --> 00:11:24.820
removed from the aircraft.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:27.690
Six others from his French class are also
removed in the commotion.

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:30.760
Alex’s foresight comes true, and Sam and
Molly perish in the crash.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:34.620
A piece of the aircraft flies back towards
the city and crushes Nathan and several others,

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:37.180
completing Death’s list from the North Bay
Bridge collapse.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:40.990
But because 6 of the Mt. Abraham High School
students and one teacher got off the plane

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:44.800
that they should have died on, Death must
start a new list to clean up these survivors.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.300
At this point, you probably have a lot of
questions.

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:51.050
The previous disasters that I’ve talked
about have been relatively self contained.

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:54.870
So if Sam had never had a vision, and the
Presage Paper employees had died on the bridge

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:57.630
collapse, would Flight 180 still have needed
to crash?

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:00.180
Or did Death take Sam’s vision into account?

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:03.580
Was the plan all along for him to survive
the bridge collapse so that he could die on

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:04.580
Flight 180?

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:08.080
The way I see it, once your time is up, your
time is up, and when that time comes, you

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:12.050
may be able to put it off a little bit, but
you really can’t change history; you can’t

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:13.050
alter the bigger picture.

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:16.580
I’ll be able to fully explain why by the
end of the video, but for now, think of it

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:17.580
like this.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:20.670
If Sam had never had his vision, the Presage
employees would have died on the bridge, but

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:24.930
Flight 180 was always destined to crash whether
their seats were filled or not.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:29.270
Because Sam and Molly did survive, Death altered
its schemes just slightly to put them on Flight

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:31.230
180, which was going to crash anyway.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:35.510
From here, it just gets more and more complicated,
because Death’s new plans for the Mt. Abraham

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:39.750
students create a butterfly effect resulting
in new survivors, to be added to Death’s

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:44.770
growing list, as well as other disasters in
different parts of the world.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:51.460
One of coolest things about Hunt a Killer's
Blair Witch game, is that you receive these

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:55.890
boxes of evidence and solve the mystery entirely
from home, but you still have that sense of

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:56.890
exploration.

00:12:56.890 --> 00:13:00.500
They do such a good job a building this world,
you end up becoming totally immersed in these

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.330
locations and attached to the characters you're
trying to help.

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:07.190
If you love the slow burn pit in your stomach
type of horror, this is the alternate reality

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:08.190
game for you.

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:11.750
The story unfolds a little bit more with each
box, making it a satisfying adventure to take

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:15.300
on with a partner, but an equally rewarding
endeavor to solve on your own.

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:17.730
Just don't come crying to me if the Blair
Witch ends up in your nightmares.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:18.911
Actually, on second thought.

00:13:18.911 --> 00:13:20.430
I do want to know if that happens.

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:23.920
There's even an optional, spoiler-free online
community where you can collaborate with other

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:27.860
detectives to try solve difficult puzzles
or share your own theories about the characters

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:28.860
in the story.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:34.659
This is your chance -- go to HuntAKiller.com/CZsWorld
and use CODE CZSWORLD, for 20% off your that

00:13:34.659 --> 00:13:35.659
first box.

00:13:35.659 --> 00:13:36.159
Again.

00:13:36.159 --> 00:13:36.739
CODE CZSWORLD.

00:13:36.739 --> 00:13:38.199
Twenty percent discount.

00:13:38.199 --> 00:13:39.779
What else could you really ask for?

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:48.860
Alex Browning’s best friend Tod Waggner
is first up on Death’s new list, but before

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:52.490
Death reaches him, it’s likely that he did
something to extend the life of a man named

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.450
Evan Lewis, but we don’t really know exactly what.

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:58.610
All we do know is that Evan is added to a
new list, that Death would deal with later.

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:02.720
In June of 2000, Tod slips on some leaked
toilet water in his bathroom, ultimately causing

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:05.500
him to accidentally strangle himself on this
clothesline.

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:09.070
This is the point where I’d say we have
proof that Death is a force of nature, but

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:13.510
also a character, a grim reaper trying to
outsmart its victims, because after killing

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:17.450
Tod, it cleans up after itself by receding
toilet water to make Tod’s death look like

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:18.450
a suicide.

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:21.990
This was likely to throw off William Bludworth,
who was now giving advice to some of the accident

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:22.990
survivors.

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:24.860
Death didn’t want Bludworth metaling with
its plans.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:28.690
It doesn’t work though, Bludworth is still
able to determine the real cause of Tod’s

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:29.690
death.

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:32.610
This tells me that Death is powerful, but
not perfect, and Bludworth’s teachings to

00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:36.660
Flight 180 survivor Clear Rivers would continue
to be a problem for Death going forward.

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:40.730
The next Flight 180 student that Death reaches
is Terry Chaney, who is hit by a bus, but

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:45.050
this also causes a woman named Kat Jennings,
who was on that bus, not to reach the hotel

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:49.240
she was supposed to die at, so she is now
added to the second list behind Evan Lewis.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.390
Death goes after the teacher that got off
of Flight 180, Valerie Lewton, by blowing

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:56.030
up her computer monitor, setting her home
on fire, and finally letting her drop a kitchen

00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:57.440
knife into her own body.

00:14:57.440 --> 00:15:01.180
Later that night, Alex saves his classmate
Carter Horton from being hit by a train.

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:04.630
Death skips Carter and moves onto the next
in line, Billy Hitchcock, who is killed by

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.221
a piece of scrap metal that shoots out from
under the train.

00:15:07.221 --> 00:15:10.680
A police officer named Thomas Burke is dispatched
to investigate Billy’s death, causing him

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.470
not to be there for a shootout that kills
his partner.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.791
Since Burke was also supposed to die in the
shootout, he is added to Death’s second

00:15:16.791 --> 00:15:17.791
list.

00:15:17.791 --> 00:15:20.990
The next day, a teacher named Eugene Dix is
called in to substitute for Ms. Lewton’s

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:24.280
class, causing him to be absent during an
attack that took place at the school he would

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:27.870
have otherwise been teaching at, so he too
is added to the second list.

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:31.550
It seems like Death is just letting this second
list grow until after it’s taken care of

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:32.550
the first list.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:36.780
At some point Nora and Tim Carpenter are also
added to the second list, probably as a ripple

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:39.100
effect of something Alex Browning did.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:42.000
Something he would not have been able to do
if he had died on Flight 180.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:46.410
The next victim is Clear Rivers, but Alex
manages to save her, so the target moves to

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:47.410
him.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.200
Six months go by before Death makes another
attempt.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:52.430
With Clear’s warning and Carter’s quick
action, Alex’s life is saved.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:55.370
Death cycles back through the list, so it’s
once again Carter’s turn.

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:58.645
He isn’t so lucky and he’s struck by a
fallen restaurant sign.

00:15:58.659 --> 00:16:06.210
The commotion causes Rory Peters, who is nearby, to miss his show at a local theater, which would later collapse, and he would also be added to the second list.

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:10.420
Death makes dozens of attempts, going back
and forth between Clear and Alex, before finally,

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:12.820
Alex is knocked out of the picture by a falling
brick.

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.790
Clear goes into hiding in a padded room where
Death is unable to reach her.

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:19.370
This is another reason I think Death is more
of a character making conscious decisions,

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:22.810
because if it were simply a set of rules,
it wouldn’t move on to that second list

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:24.630
until Clear was taken care of.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:28.050
But with Clear locked away in isolation, it
didn’t really matter if Death focused on

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:31.730
other things, because she was unlikely to
save any other lives while she was in there,

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:34.380
and if she did come out, Death would have
an opportunity to finish her.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:37.801
But before that happens, is when I believe
the events of Final Destination: Spring Break

00:16:37.801 --> 00:16:38.801
take place.

00:16:38.801 --> 00:16:42.110
We know this happens around March, because
that’s when Spring Breaks tend to happen.

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:45.330
I think it’s in the year 2001 because it
seems to be after Flight 180.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:49.290
There’s a point where a character sees that
her flight is also 180 and her eyes go wide.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:51.600
But it can’t be too far into the 21st century.

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:54.350
They still have standard definition TVs in
the hotels.

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:58.860
Carly Hagan and her friends are vacationing
at the Hotel Grand Tzolk'in in Cancun, Mexico.

00:16:58.860 --> 00:17:01.690
Before arriving, she has a premonition of
her hotel exploding.

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:05.059
When she sees the signs from her dream starting
to come true, she urges her friends to go

00:17:05.059 --> 00:17:06.120
outside with her.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:09.550
Because it’s her birthday wish, they do,
just in time so see the explosion that would

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:10.550
have killed them.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.890
Throughout the rest of the vacation, Death
comes for each of them.

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.789
Kris is chopped up by a boat propeller.

00:17:14.789 --> 00:17:17.819
His girlfriend Katie breaks a thermometer
on herself and then trips and falls on some

00:17:17.819 --> 00:17:19.100
sharp skeleton bones.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:21.779
Gino crashes through a glass bottom boat while
scuba diving.

00:17:21.779 --> 00:17:25.579
Dreena tries to leave Cancun, but falls off
the jet bridge after it’s struck by a runaway

00:17:25.579 --> 00:17:26.579
forklift.

00:17:26.579 --> 00:17:28.139
Jeremy falls down during this and also dies.

00:17:28.139 --> 00:17:30.740
They’re unable to leave the country with
an incoming Hurricane.

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:33.820
Amanda drowns when the automatic pool cover
turns on while she’s swimming underwater.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:36.529
Matt’s abs are not strong enough to stand
up to fireworks.

00:17:36.529 --> 00:17:38.440
Jake is chopped up by a rescue helicopter.

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:41.540
Bryan tries to hide from the Hurricane in
a coffin, but he never manages to make it out.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:42.360
And Carly…

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:44.240
Well, I’m not sure exactly what happens to her.

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:47.970
She sees the creepy Shaman in the mirror,
and then… she just kind of disappears.

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:49.110
I don’t know.

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:50.320
Dust in the wind I guess.

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:54.129
After soaking up the sun in Cancun, Death
returns to New York, still needing to take

00:17:54.129 --> 00:17:58.019
care of that second list, and see if anything
can be done about the hermit, Clear Rivers.

00:17:58.019 --> 00:18:01.919
But before doing that, there are a couple
more disasters with unintended survivors.

00:18:01.919 --> 00:18:04.920
One involved 38 year old Doris Fenwick, who
is saved from drowning.

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:07.980
Her fate after that is unknown, but we can
assume Death comes for her.

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:11.590
The other is a larger incident that becomes
known as the infamous Lakeview fire.

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:14.639
We don’t know if it was a premonition that
caused some of the victims to survive this

00:18:14.639 --> 00:18:17.850
time, but given the track record of the series,
it probably was.

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:21.610
All of the survivors passed away in what is
described as an eerie string of deaths, but

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:24.639
one of the last survivors was a teenager named
Brian Gibbons.

00:18:24.639 --> 00:18:28.730
However, before taking out Brian, Death decides
now is a good time to try to reclaim the lives

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:33.150
of Evan, Tim, Nora, Kat, Rory, Eugene, Clear
and Thomas.

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:36.250
Clear is still in the padded room though,
so she’s off the board for now, so Death’s

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:39.250
new plan is to take out all the others in
a massive highway pileup.

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:42.559
I’ll also note that the order they were
going to die in during the pile up doesn’t

00:18:42.559 --> 00:18:46.100
match up with the order in which they were
interfered with by the would-be Flight 180

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.120
victims, because that order isn’t necessarily
the order they would have died in.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.910
If that explanation sounds confusing, think
about it like this.

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:55.690
Burke could have gotten shot in that shoot
out, but not died from his injuries for another

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:56.690
couple days.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.379
We don’t know, because we don’t see any
of that.

00:18:58.379 --> 00:19:01.120
What I’m trying to say is just don’t worry too much
about the order here.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:04.770
Death’s designs are thwarted once again
by William Bludworth, who seems to somehow

00:19:04.770 --> 00:19:07.970
make contact with a young woman named Kimberly
Corman…

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:12.397
just before her very own Flight
180 style premonition.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:25.480
Kimberly’s vision not only saves those who
were on that second death list, but also herself,

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:27.370
leading her to basically just be added to
that list.

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:29.590
Also, Death starts working backwards at this
point.

00:19:29.590 --> 00:19:33.620
So the last one that should have died in the
Route 23 pile up, Kimberly, is now the first

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:34.620
target.

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:36.340
Why does Death decide to go in reverse here?

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:39.600
This is twice that this set of victims have
gotten away, so it might be to try to catch

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:40.600
them off guard.

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:44.269
Flight 180 has become kind of a mainstream
story at this point, and maybe Death is worried

00:19:44.269 --> 00:19:46.620
that the victims are figuring out its MO.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:50.009
Death comes for Kimberly immediately in the
form of a barreling truck, but Officer Burke

00:19:50.009 --> 00:19:52.550
pulls her out of the way, so her spot is skipped
for now.

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:56.159
Evan is crushed by a ladder, Tim is crushed
by a glass pane and Nora is decapitated by

00:19:56.159 --> 00:19:57.159
an elevator.

00:19:57.159 --> 00:20:00.809
Eugene tries to just give up and take himself
out, but he’s physically unable to do so

00:20:00.809 --> 00:20:04.740
because it isn’t his turn, as explained
by Clear, who is now helping the new victims.

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:08.419
I’m not really a fan of this rule, but it
doesn’t matter, this is how it is.

00:20:08.419 --> 00:20:11.929
You literally cannot die until death has decided
it’s your turn.

00:20:11.929 --> 00:20:12.929
And it’s Kat’s turn.

00:20:12.929 --> 00:20:15.559
Her airbag goes off, sending her head into
a sharp pipe.

00:20:15.559 --> 00:20:19.260
Rory actually encounters the Lakeview fire
survivor, Brian Gibbons, and saves him from

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:22.440
being hit by a news van, thus extending his
life a little bit longer.

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:25.950
Then, we see the importance of Death taking
them out in the correct order again, because

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:29.649
it actually knocks down a tree branch in order
to move Burke out of the way so he isn’t

00:20:29.649 --> 00:20:32.240
hit by the barbed wire fence that slices through
Rory.

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:36.309
Next up is Eugene, who is taken out in an
explosion that also incinerates Clear.

00:20:36.309 --> 00:20:39.750
Now you might ask why Clear was able to die
right here if it isn’t her turn?

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.760
I think it’s because she’s technically
still on the Flight 180 list.

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:43.760
Not the Route 23 list.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:47.240
So on that list, it’s been her turn the
entire time; she’s the last one.

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:51.159
With a last ditch plan, Kimberly decides to
drive into a lake, hoping that because she’s

00:20:51.159 --> 00:20:54.470
next to the hospital, she would be treated
quickly and someone would be able to revive

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:55.470
her.

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:58.759
This would theoretically invalidate Death’s
list, according to what she was told by Bludworth…

00:20:58.759 --> 00:21:00.799
...and her and Burke would be saved.

00:21:00.799 --> 00:21:03.059
This is the second theory proposed by Bludworth.

00:21:03.059 --> 00:21:06.370
This one actually has a little bit more going
for it, because we’ve now seen Patti Fuller’s

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:10.749
grandmother, Patti Fuller herself, Louise
King and now Kimberly Corman all survive using

00:21:10.749 --> 00:21:11.749
this tactic.

00:21:11.749 --> 00:21:15.210
It’s possible that they all died shortly
after, but none of them are confirmed dead.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.730
In fact, Kimberly and Burke reunite with the
Gibbons family for a barbecue at the end of

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:23.320
that summer in 2001, and the grill explodes
on Brian, thus wrapping up the list of victims

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:24.320
from the Lakeview fire.

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:27.370
It would be a couple more years until Death
would have to start another list.

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:31.120
I mean, obviously this kind of stuff is probably
always happening off screen, but the next

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:36.009
Final Destination story would be Final Destination:
Death of the Senses taking place in 2003,

00:21:36.009 --> 00:21:37.596
a few years after Flight 180.

00:21:37.596 --> 00:21:41.237
Jack Curtis was the driver of the bus that
ran over Terry Chaney in 2000.

00:21:41.237 --> 00:21:43.318
You know, the one that Kat was also on.

00:21:43.318 --> 00:21:45.679
He would lose his job because of this, and
become homeless.

00:21:45.679 --> 00:21:49.140
And it is because he is homeless that he’s
in the right place at the right time to save

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:52.009
a police officer named Amy Tom from a serial
killer.

00:21:52.009 --> 00:21:55.430
That means all the victims that the serial
killer would have gotten are now safe, so

00:21:55.430 --> 00:21:57.440
Death has to take out each of them.

00:21:57.440 --> 00:22:01.590
The serial killer is referred to as John Doe,
and yes, he’s very similar to the John Doe

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:05.940
from Se7en, but instead of basing his crimes
on The Seven Deadly sins, he planned to base

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:07.309
them on the five senses.

00:22:07.309 --> 00:22:10.480
For sight, he was to take out a beautiful
reporter named Chelsea Cox.

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:11.700
Death gets her with an icicle.

00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:12.340
On the air!

00:22:12.340 --> 00:22:13.420
"WE'LL DO IT LIVE! F-"

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:17.529
For smell, the target was the man in charge
of municipal trash collection, Dawson Donahue.

00:22:17.529 --> 00:22:18.800
His car explodes.

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:21.190
Taste was going to be food critic Dominique Swann.

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:23.820
Death blows up her wine bottle and she’s
choked by a glass shard.

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:27.840
Touch would have been Katie Astin, a talk
show host and televangelist, who was electrocuted.

00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:32.090
And for sound, the victim would have been
Joshua Cornell III, a rapper-producer whose

00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:35.500
head is cut off when his platinum record is
launched through the air during an equipment

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:36.500
malfunction.

00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:40.309
Of course, there is one more, and that is
the officer that Jack saved: Amy Tom.

00:22:40.309 --> 00:22:44.320
She is impaled by her own art piece, and then
Jack also dies even though he wasn’t technically

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:47.269
on the list, because Officer Tom’s partner
thought that he was the killer.

00:22:47.269 --> 00:22:48.269
Oopsie!

00:22:48.269 --> 00:22:52.100
On May 13th 2005, the five year anniversary
of Flight 180, and the four year anniversary

00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:54.960
of the Route 23 pile up, there are two more
psychic visions.

00:22:54.960 --> 00:22:58.570
I would definitely understand if this is becoming
one of Death’s least favorite days of the

00:22:58.570 --> 00:22:59.570
year.

00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:02.169
The first is in Miami during Final Destination:
Looks Could Kill.

00:23:02.169 --> 00:23:06.019
Woman named Stephanie Pulaski (also known
as Sherry) is part of a modeling group called

00:23:06.019 --> 00:23:08.950
“Cellar” where each model is nicknamed
after a different type of wine.

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:12.559
During a party on a yacht called the Coral
Clipper, Sherry has a vision of a fatal crash,

00:23:12.559 --> 00:23:16.399
and she convinces her boyfriend and some of
the other models to exit the boat before it

00:23:16.399 --> 00:23:17.399
departs.

00:23:17.399 --> 00:23:20.009
When the crash occurs for real, a piece of
debris strikes Sherry in the face, sending

00:23:20.009 --> 00:23:21.009
her into a coma.

00:23:21.009 --> 00:23:25.169
While she was being hospitalized, a similar
disaster would occur further up the Atlantic

00:23:25.169 --> 00:23:29.707
coast during a special grad night at McKinley
Park.

00:23:37.130 --> 00:23:41.879
That night in McKinley, Pennsylvania, a yearbook
photographer named Wendy Christensen has a

00:23:41.879 --> 00:23:44.750
vision about a horrific accident on a roller
coaster called Devil’s Flight.

00:23:44.750 --> 00:23:48.419
She causes a scene and several other high
school students get off the ride before it

00:23:48.419 --> 00:23:52.100
crashes, but Wendy loses her boyfriend and
her best friend, because their car’s restraints

00:23:52.100 --> 00:23:53.160
were not released.

00:23:53.160 --> 00:23:57.010
Wendy sees the ominous signs of Death in her
photographs from that night and tries to figure

00:23:57.010 --> 00:24:00.629
out their meaning so she can warn each of
the others before they are crossed off of

00:24:00.629 --> 00:24:01.919
Death’s newest checklist.

00:24:01.919 --> 00:24:06.309
Popular girls Ashley Freund and Ashlyn Halperin
both become victims of a tanning bed incident,

00:24:06.309 --> 00:24:09.840
pervert Frankie Cheeks becomes a Motorhead…
and not in the heavy metal kind of way -- and

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:12.970
football star Lewis Romero is all brawns and
no brain…

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:15.850
literally because his head is crushed by a
pair of giant weights.

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:19.440
Wendy and her friend Kevin Fischer are able
to prevent the death of Ian McKinley, so the

00:24:19.440 --> 00:24:22.510
next target is his girlfriend Erin, who is
spiked by a nail gun.

00:24:22.510 --> 00:24:26.009
Wendy’s sister Julie was also on the ride,
and with the help of Kevin, Wendy’s able

00:24:26.009 --> 00:24:29.980
to rescue her, but her friend Perry is not
so lucky and gets impaled by a flagpole.

00:24:29.980 --> 00:24:33.679
Wendy and Kevin are both able to dodge death,
so it comes back around to Ian, who is crushed

00:24:33.679 --> 00:24:34.890
by a falling sign.

00:24:34.890 --> 00:24:37.740
So Wendy, Kevin and Julie are safe… for
now...

00:24:37.740 --> 00:24:42.320
In August 2005, Sherry is released from the
hospital stay that began with the yacht crash,

00:24:42.320 --> 00:24:46.019
but she’s forced to wear a mask to cover
her now disfigured face, and she thinks her

00:24:46.019 --> 00:24:47.019
life is over.

00:24:47.019 --> 00:24:49.610
But like Eugene, she’s unable to end it
herself.

00:24:49.610 --> 00:24:52.952
She then receives a phone call from Death,
or at the very least, someone or something

00:24:52.952 --> 00:24:55.530
posing as Death, who offers to make her a
deal.

00:24:55.530 --> 00:24:59.159
We’ve never seen Death be compromising or
try to make a deal with any of the victims

00:24:59.159 --> 00:25:02.639
in the series, so I think it stands to reason
that this caller is an imposter.

00:25:02.639 --> 00:25:05.890
They meet at a café, where he appears as
an elderly black man.

00:25:05.890 --> 00:25:08.830
He asks her to help get rid of the survivors
that should have drowned that day.

00:25:08.830 --> 00:25:11.190
In exchange for that, he would restore her
face.

00:25:11.190 --> 00:25:14.879
Not only has Death not taken a human form
before, but it’s never really needed help

00:25:14.879 --> 00:25:15.879
killing anyone.

00:25:15.879 --> 00:25:18.710
A fellow model named Chablis is eaten away
by spilled chemicals.

00:25:18.710 --> 00:25:22.429
Shiraz’s scalp is torn off and her head
is twisted around on a music video set.

00:25:22.429 --> 00:25:24.509
Chardonnay hits her head and drowns in a hot
tub.

00:25:24.509 --> 00:25:27.429
Rose’s organs are vacuumed in a botched
liposuction surgery.

00:25:27.429 --> 00:25:30.950
Sherry’s boyfriend, Brut, is run over by
a subway train after falling into a manhole.

00:25:30.950 --> 00:25:34.419
And a photographer named Gunter was crushed
after being pinned by the loading platform

00:25:34.419 --> 00:25:35.419
of a delivery truck.

00:25:35.419 --> 00:25:39.669
For each of these deaths, Sherry has either
played a hand, or watched idly as they happen.

00:25:39.669 --> 00:25:43.059
But she can’t bring herself to kill her
best friend Cabernet, and because of this,

00:25:43.059 --> 00:25:44.150
she’s broken the deal.

00:25:44.150 --> 00:25:47.909
Cabernet is also pregnant, and the delivery
of her child may be what saves her.

00:25:47.909 --> 00:25:48.909
Remember the clue...

00:25:50.610 --> 00:25:54.049
“Only new life can defeat Death.

00:25:54.049 --> 00:25:58.900
The introduction of life that was not meant
to be… that can invalidate the list.

00:25:58.900 --> 00:26:01.450
Force Death to start anew.”

00:26:01.450 --> 00:26:05.440
We’ve only seen the “new life can defeat
Death” cheat used successfully for people

00:26:05.440 --> 00:26:09.529
who were revived, but back in Final Destination
2, Kimberly’s original understanding of

00:26:09.529 --> 00:26:13.139
this clue was that if someone who was supposed
to have died creates new life by giving birth,

00:26:13.139 --> 00:26:15.110
they would essentially be off the hook.

00:26:15.110 --> 00:26:18.820
Anyways, after publicly screaming about her
deal with Death, Sherry is admitted to a psych

00:26:18.820 --> 00:26:19.820
ward.

00:26:19.820 --> 00:26:22.850
In November, Wendy and Kevin are now in college,
and Julie meets both of them by chance on

00:26:22.850 --> 00:26:24.960
the subway when Wendy has another vision.

00:26:24.960 --> 00:26:28.299
This time, she sees their train crashing,
but unlike the roller coaster, they aren’t

00:26:28.299 --> 00:26:29.299
able to get off.

00:26:29.299 --> 00:26:33.049
We don’t see what happens after this, but
there is a possibility that some of them survived,

00:26:33.049 --> 00:26:36.950
since every other vision in the series has
resulted in at least one person being saved,

00:26:36.950 --> 00:26:40.580
so it stands to reason that these visions
are always a clue about how to avoid the hand

00:26:40.580 --> 00:26:41.580
of death.

00:26:41.580 --> 00:26:45.610
During the six months that follow Sherry gets
better, and even goes through a facial reconstruction

00:26:45.610 --> 00:26:46.610
program.

00:26:46.610 --> 00:26:50.789
On May 13th 2006, Sherry is crossing a street
to meet up with Cabernet when she receives

00:26:50.789 --> 00:26:51.789
a phone call.

00:26:51.789 --> 00:26:55.690
The caller ID simply says: Death, and Sherry
is struck down by a bus.

00:26:55.690 --> 00:27:00.600
As you can probably tell, Death seems to be
a gearhead, and loves vehicular accidents.

00:27:00.600 --> 00:27:01.970
Just freaking adores them.

00:27:01.970 --> 00:27:05.919
So in 2009, the most vehicle oriented disaster
of them all would occur.

00:27:05.919 --> 00:27:10.850
The Megatech 300 would be held at the McKinley
Speedway, where a… guy… we don’t really

00:27:10.850 --> 00:27:14.950
know what he does, named Nick O’Bannon would
experience his own Flight 180 phenomenon.

00:27:14.950 --> 00:27:18.820
He envisions a huge pile up where race cars
crash and tumble into the stands, taking out

00:27:18.820 --> 00:27:21.550
many fans, so he pulls his friends away from
the action.

00:27:21.550 --> 00:27:25.460
In doing so, he inadvertently starts a fight
and is chased out of the stadium by several

00:27:25.460 --> 00:27:26.460
people.

00:27:26.460 --> 00:27:29.249
Their lives are saved when his vision comes
true, but Death gets to work quickly.

00:27:29.249 --> 00:27:33.200
A woman named Nadia is obliterated by a flying
tire, Carter Daniels is dragged down the street

00:27:33.200 --> 00:27:36.889
and lit on fire by his leaking truck, Samantha
is shot in the eye when a lawnmower ejects

00:27:36.889 --> 00:27:38.830
a rock, and Andy is diced by a fence.

00:27:38.830 --> 00:27:42.080
Nearby, there’s kind of a side disaster
that happens nearby, when an out of control

00:27:42.080 --> 00:27:46.009
truck crashes into a coffee shop and runs
over three McKinley High School students.

00:27:46.009 --> 00:27:49.570
Nick’s friend Janet is able to avoid Death’s
first attack at the car wash, but their friend

00:27:49.570 --> 00:27:52.990
Hunt is not so lucky, as he’s drowned and
sucked into a pool drain.

00:27:52.990 --> 00:27:56.490
A man named Jonathan Groves is crushed by
a bathtub that falls through from a floor

00:27:56.490 --> 00:27:59.890
above at the hospital, just like Rinoka from
Final Destination: End of the Line, and a

00:27:59.890 --> 00:28:02.269
security guard named George is hit by an ambulance.

00:28:02.269 --> 00:28:06.139
Just like seemingly half of the population
in this franchise being killed by vehicles.

00:28:06.139 --> 00:28:09.390
The remaining three are Nick, his girlfriend
Lori and their friend Janet.

00:28:09.390 --> 00:28:12.890
Nick has a new vision, which leads him to
save the girls from an exploding movie theater,

00:28:12.890 --> 00:28:16.779
so Death goes back to one of it’s most reliable
methods, and hits them with a truck.

00:28:16.779 --> 00:28:19.960
At the time of making this video, this is
the last major death to occur.

00:28:19.960 --> 00:28:25.129
So, by going through literally everything,
all 1,458 confirmed kills -- and that’s

00:28:25.129 --> 00:28:28.310
not including Carly -- we’ve learned a lot
about the rules and tendencies of Death, but

00:28:28.310 --> 00:28:32.700
like the actual concept of death in real life,
there are still some things that we’ll never

00:28:32.700 --> 00:28:33.700
understand.

00:28:33.700 --> 00:28:36.510
However, in looking at the bigger picture,
we can get a better idea of how this all works.

00:28:36.510 --> 00:28:37.630
Here’s what I’ve gathered.

00:28:37.630 --> 00:28:38.860
Death is unstoppable.

00:28:38.860 --> 00:28:42.100
The only way you may be able to avoid it is
with the introduction of new life that was

00:28:42.100 --> 00:28:45.440
never meant to be, but since we never see
any of the characters who tried this later

00:28:45.440 --> 00:28:48.510
on down the line, we can’t say with 100%
certainty that this works.

00:28:48.510 --> 00:28:50.860
So you can’t avoid it, but you can put it
off.

00:28:50.860 --> 00:28:53.600
But if you do cheat Death, don’t expect
it to last long.

00:28:53.600 --> 00:28:57.250
The only one who survived for an extended
period was Clear, and she did so by locking

00:28:57.250 --> 00:29:00.990
herself away and not really interacting with
anyone, thus not doing anything to change

00:29:00.990 --> 00:29:02.860
the course of history in a major way.

00:29:02.860 --> 00:29:07.340
The best comparison I can make to the nature
of the Flight 180 phenomenon, is Stephen King’s

00:29:07.340 --> 00:29:08.340
11/22/63.

00:29:08.340 --> 00:29:11.830
That story involves a teacher named Jake Epping
who goes back in time to try to prevent the

00:29:11.830 --> 00:29:13.690
assassination of John F Kennedy.

00:29:13.690 --> 00:29:16.909
But he also tries to fix other things while
he’s in the past, which he believes will

00:29:16.909 --> 00:29:18.610
make the world a better place in the present.

00:29:18.610 --> 00:29:22.940
But whenever he tries to change history, the
universe fights back, and “corrects” whatever

00:29:22.940 --> 00:29:23.940
he does.

00:29:23.940 --> 00:29:27.879
And this makes it very difficult for him to
change a major historical event, like a presidential

00:29:27.879 --> 00:29:28.879
assassination.

00:29:28.879 --> 00:29:32.659
So in essence, he’s able to change little
details, but things just get smoothed over

00:29:32.659 --> 00:29:34.619
and eventually go unnoticed.

00:29:34.619 --> 00:29:37.269
He can’t do much to change the destiny of
the universe.

00:29:37.269 --> 00:29:40.279
And I think this is basically how it goes in Final
Destination.

00:29:40.279 --> 00:29:43.649
If you have a vision about the future, you
may be able to save yourself for the time

00:29:43.649 --> 00:29:48.330
being, but before long, Death will correct
your actions, and you will be the one to pay

00:29:48.330 --> 00:29:49.330
the price for it.

00:29:49.330 --> 00:29:53.519
Click the video on the left to see my analysis
of other Final Destination characters, and

00:29:53.519 --> 00:29:57.860
if you love horror remember to subscribe to
CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:29:57.860 --> 00:30:01.919
the deathbell for notifications and I’ll
see you in the next one.

00:30:01.919 --> 00:30:04.080
Assuming we both survive.

00:30:04.080 --> 00:30:08.228
If you want to actually beat death, use a
facemask and social distancing.

